- Using TDD for business behavior.
- Running relevant verification after edits.
- Recording actual results.
- Updating AI governance files after meaningful work.
- Avoiding scope creep.
- Challenging conflicting or risky requests.
- Never fabricating evidence.
- Never storing secrets or hidden chain-of-thought.
- Keeping one active task.
- Keeping NEXT.md accurate and concise.
- Not declaring work complete when required checks fail.

==================================================
22. TASK COMPLETION DEFINITION
==================================================

A task is DONE only when:

- Acceptance criteria are satisfied.
- Relevant tests pass.
- Type checking passes.
- Linting passes.
- Formatting checks pass.
- Documentation is updated where required.
- Test evidence is recorded.
- Memory remains accurate.
- The task is moved to completed.json.
- NEXT.md identifies the next action.

If verification cannot run, keep the task out of DONE and document the blocker.

